  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## v1.13.0 (minor)\n\nChanges since v1.12.0:\n\n- Refuse an out-of-range --port with one line instead of a Kestrel stack trace [patch] (#155) (matt-edmondson)\n- Rewrite an action whose upstream expires_in is 0, as git-lfs reads it as unset [patch] (#157) (matt-edmondson)\n- Keep a configured Kestrel endpoint unless --port is given [patch] (#141) (matt-edmondson)\n- Refuse a follower timeout, refresh timeout or maintenance interval a timer can't hold [patch] (#151) (matt-edmondson)\n- Record each lock snapshot's size and count walks over the lock ceiling [minor] (#145) (matt-edmondson)\n- Count the bytes and objects each eviction sweep deletes [minor] (#144) (matt-edmondson)\n- Treat a zero-time expires_at as no expiry when rewriting batch actions [patch] (Claude)\n- Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into fix/retry-after-http-date (matt-edmondson)\n- Cap the upstream throttle pause so one Retry-After cannot stall batched locking [patch] (matt-edmondson)\n- Treat an HTTP-date Retry-After as a throttle in the lock fan-out [patch] (matt-edmondson)\n- Never advertise expires_in 0 for a short-lived upstream action [patch] (matt-edmondson)\n- Relay a body with its length, and keep a lock time's plus sign unescaped [patch] (matt-edmondson)\n- Refuse a backslash in the request path so it cannot escape the upstream prefix [patch] (Claude)\n- Raise ktsu.Essentials to 2.10.7 and Testably interface to 10.4.0 (Claude)\n- Merge main into dependabot/nuget/Testably.Abstractions.Testing-7.1.1 (Claude)\n- Count follower attempts in a while loop so its condition and counter agree (Claude)\n- Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into fix/62-range-on-cache-hit (Claude)\n- Hand an aborted leader's fetch to one follower instead of all of them [patch] (Claude)\n- Store objects for an upstream key with a dot in it, such as gitlab.com [patch] (Claude)\n- Expire a batch action's proxy token no later than upstream's href [patch] (Claude)\n- Serve a Range request for a cached object as 206 instead of the whole object [patch] (Claude)\n- Cover the --store override inside the command action (Claude)\n- Answer 502, not 500, when upstream's 2xx batch body cannot be used [patch] (Claude)\n- Resolve a relative --store path instead of aborting startup [patch] (Claude)\n- Refuse a locks/batch ref that is not an object with 400 instead of 500 [patch] (Claude)\n- Lift the request body limit on the transfer route so large pushes go through [patch] (Claude)",
